-For external checkpoint/restore orchestrators, available with `--enable-sleep-mode`. Preparing drains the engine and releases its KV cache and other external state, any number of times. Until `/checkpoint/restore`, new requests get a retryable error and `/health` still returns 200, as while asleep. `--checkpoint-prepare-on-startup` prepares each engine once it starts. With a KV connector, the engine prepares only if the connector supports it. `NixlConnector` in pull mode needs `--checkpoint-prepare-on-startup`. Each restore appends a random suffix to the KV engine id, so restored replicas get distinct `remote_engine_id` values.
